<!--CLI Documentation — DualCliModel
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation.DualCliModel-->
<clidoc:DualCliModel xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:clidoc="com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Universal CLI versus the MachineBlocks host
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Two commands, one compiler.

    @blockml/cli (command: blockml), library org.blockml.bml.cli.*:
    - Universal toolchain: validate, compile blockdoc or xsd or fatblock, search,
      graph, inspect, transform, new, init, update.
    - Domain-agnostic. No MachineBlocks paths, no machineblocks-v3-scad built-in.
    - Reads blockml.config.json targets[] for toolchain targets.
    - Scope exclusions in that library list machineblocks-v3-scad registration
      as out of scope on purpose.

    @machineblocks/cli (this package), library com.machineblocks.bml.cli.*:
    - Thin host. Recommended entry for MachineBlocks users.
    - Registers machineblocks-v3-scad by constructing the render target with a
      BlockRenderEngine.
    - Same validate and compile facade underneath. Defaults differ.
    - Does not reimplement parse, validate, or emit.
    - init calls initProject from @blockml/cli with noInstall. That call runs
      preflight before any write, including the foreign AGENTS.md rename.
      Then this host adds dependency @machineblocks/core beside @blockml/core,
      devDependency @machineblocks/cli, and library dependency
      com.machineblocks.bml.Library. Unless --no-install, it then
      runs npm install and GenerateAgentsMd, which overwrites AGENTS.md.
      Profile first, then the same install and AGENTS.md step as initProject.
      --no-install does not skip preflight. The universal init stays
      domain-agnostic.
    - update rewrites @machineblocks/cli, @machineblocks/core, @blockml/cli, and
      @blockml/core in an existing project's package.json to the versions of
      this host, then runs npm install. It does not call updateProject. A
      specifier that contains ":" stays. BML files, AGENTS.md, and CLAUDE.md
      stay. --no-install skips npm install. The universal update stays on
      blockml and pins only @blockml/cli and @blockml/core.

    Interop: a later plugin load (targetPackages in blockml.config.json mapping
    machineblocks-v3-scad to @machineblocks/render-target) may let the universal
    CLI see the target. Product UX stays on this host either way. The universal
    CLI must keep working for projects that never install MachineBlocks.

    Ownership:
    - This package owns the host bin, MachineBlocks defaults, and target registration.
    - @blockml/compiler owns compileToOutput, CompileRequest, and the registry API.
    - @machineblocks/render-target owns processors and SCAD emit.
    - @blockml/block-render-engine owns strategy infrastructure.
    - Thumbnail generation (OpenSCAD plus image tooling) is a host concern when
      it is built; it is not part of @blockml/cli V1.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidoc:Responsibilities" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</clidoc:DualCliModel>
